    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a condensed starting core, as stalwarts **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are all idle due to scheduled off-days, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. In their absence, **Sam Antonacci** emerges as our highest-graded start (44.04). Despite the challenging matchup against Williams, G (xERA 2.95), **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s leadoff position and favorable platoon dynamics provide a high-floor opportunity for run generation and stolen base potential, which we are heavily prioritizing given the league\u2019s scarcity. **Brayan Rocchio** (40.63) and **Miguel Vargas** (40.14) round out the daily starting trio, maintaining marginal value despite the elite-tier opposition on the mound.\n\nThe decision to bench the remaining depth pieces was largely dictated by the high concentration of elite starters on today's schedule and the preservation of our limited game caps. **Miguel Vargas** barely cleared the starting threshold; while his xwOBA of 0.378 is encouraging, the negative pressure from Williams, G\u2019s elite skill profile and a stiff 1.86s pop-time catcher limit his upside for stolen bases. We are closely monitoring the status of **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Jordan Westburg**\u2014along with developmental prospects like **Jacob Wilson** and **Coby Mayo**\u2014to ensure we aren't burning cap space during these high-difficulty pitching matchups. Caution is advised for all active starters today; the matchup against Williams, G is a defensive struggle, and any further degradation in wind conditions or late-breaking lineup changes could drop the scores of **Brayan Rocchio** and **Miguel Vargas** below our acceptable floor.",
